<div class="wrap prose">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: {{ meta.lastUpdatedLegal }}</p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>{{ brand.name }} cleans and saves pages <strong>on your computer</strong>. The pages you preview or save, your packs and your settings are never sent to us or to anyone else.</li>
    <li>There are no analytics, no tracking, no advertising and no servers of ours that receive your pages.</li>
    <li>If you buy Pro, the extension checks your licence key with Lemon Squeezy, our payment provider.</li>
    <li>Images hosted on other websites are loaded from those websites when you preview or save (you can turn this off).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>{{ brand.name }} is made by an independent developer based in {{ brand.seller.country }} ("we", "us"). Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ brand.supportEmail }}">{{ brand.supportEmail }}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What the extension does with pages</h2>
  <p>The extension reads a page only when you ask it to: by clicking its toolbar icon, using its keyboard shortcut or its right-click menu, or (Pro) using "Add all open tabs". It processes the page on your computer and stores the result — the page's text, links, its address and title, and copies of images from the page's own website — in your browser's storage on your computer. Previews you don't add to your pack are deleted after 24 hours. Pages in your pack stay until you remove them.</p>

  <h2>Images from other websites</h2>
  <p>Many websites keep their images on other servers. Those images are not copied; they are loaded directly from those servers each time you preview or save a page, just as when you view the page. Those servers can see your IP address and may receive their own cookies. The extension sends no referrer and removes invisible tracking images. You can turn images off, or turn off images from other websites, in the extension's settings.</p>

  <h2>Licence checks (Pro only)</h2>
  <p>When you enter a Pro licence key, and then about once a week, the extension sends your licence key and a random identifier for this installation to Lemon Squeezy (lemonsqueezy.com) to check that the key is valid. Lemon Squeezy sees your IP address, as with any web request. Its reply includes the name and email address on the purchase; the extension discards them immediately and does not store them. Your licence key is stored only in the extension's storage on your computer. If you use only the free features, the extension never contacts Lemon Squeezy.</p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>Lemon Squeezy is the merchant of record for {{ brand.proName }}. When you buy, you enter your name, email address and payment details on Lemon Squeezy's checkout, under <a href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/privacy">Lemon Squeezy's privacy policy</a>. We receive your name, email address, country and order details from Lemon Squeezy so we can provide support and process refunds. We never see your card details.</p>

  <h2>"Add all open tabs" (Pro)</h2>
  <p>This feature asks your browser for permission to read all websites. It is used only while adding your open tabs, and then switched off by the extension. Your browser remembers that you approved it; to withdraw the approval completely, open the browser's extensions page, find {{ brand.name }}, choose Details, and set Site access to "On click".</p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>This website uses no cookies and no analytics. It is hosted on GitHub Pages; GitHub may log visits (including IP addresses) for security, as described in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>

  <h2>Support emails</h2>
  <p>If you email us, we use your message only to help you, and delete it on request once the matter is resolved.</p>

  <h2>Legal basis, retention and your rights</h2>
  <p>For buyers, we process your purchase details to perform our contract with you and to provide support, and licence checks are in our legitimate interest in preventing misuse. Purchase records are kept as long as tax and accounting law requires, and otherwise deleted on request. You can ask to access, correct, delete or export your personal data, or object to its use, by emailing us. If you are in the EU or UK you can also complain to your data protection authority. Lemon Squeezy is based in the United States; transfers are covered by its terms and safeguards.</p>

  <h2>Your controls</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Delete all data</strong> in the extension's options removes your packs, previews and settings (your licence stays).</li>
    <li><strong>Remove licence from this computer</strong> removes your licence key from this computer and frees one of its activations.</li>
    <li>Uninstalling the extension removes all of its data from your computer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>No sale of data</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your data or use it for anything other than providing {{ brand.name }}. It is not used for advertising or credit decisions.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>{{ brand.name }} is not directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change how data is handled, we will update this page and tell you inside the extension.</p>
</div>
